Document corpus — data/docs/
================================================================================
42 documents from the CIA's declassified STARGATE collection (remote viewing
research, 1970s-1995), retrieved from the Internet Archive.

  Source:    https://archive.org  (identifiers CIA-RDP96-*)
  Origin:    US Central Intelligence Agency, released under FOIA
  Status:    Work of the US Government — public domain in the United States
             (17 U.S.C. § 105)

The full collection runs to 12,301 files and 89,901 pages. The 42 shipped here
were selected for variety of document type and for having usable OCR text; see
data/corpus_manifest.json for identifiers, titles and themes.

Text is raw OCR of scanned originals. It contains recognition errors, broken
words and page furniture. That is deliberate: it is what real retrieval
material looks like.

================================================================================
Sighting reports — data/nuforc.parquet
================================================================================
~60,000 UFO sighting reports.

  Source:    CORGIS Datasets Project, "UFO Sightings"
             https://corgis-edu.github.io/corgis/csv/ufo_sightings/
  Upstream:  Reports collected by the National UFO Reporting Center (NUFORC)
  Use:       Educational

Columns were renamed and retyped by scripts/fetch_data.py; the underlying
records are unmodified.

================================================================================
Nothing in this repository asserts that any phenomenon described in these
documents is real. The documents record what their authors claimed at the time.
Telling those two things apart is, in fact, the point of session 2.
